<title>PORTUGAL: Cimpor breaks resistance at 3,400 escudos.</title>
<headline>Cimpor breaks resistance at 3,400 escudos.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-01-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portuguese cement firm Cimpor pushed higher on confidence in the future performance of the group, breaking resistance at 3,400 escudos, dealers said.</p>
<p>&quot;There is lots of demand around for Cimpor,&quot; said one operator.</p>
<p>Another said: &quot;There is no special reason for the surge in Cimpor, except for its good fundamentals and prospects.&quot;</p>
<p>Cimpor-Cimentos de Portugal stood at 3,425 escudos, up 87, in volume of 98,690 shares at 1502 GMT.</p>
<p>-- Lisbon newsroom +351-1-3538254</p>
